# Header format: <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
# Types of commits:
# feat: Introduces a new feature.
# fix: Patches a bug.
# docs: Documentation-only changes.
# style: Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code (white-space, formatting, etc).
# refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature.
# perf: Improves performance.
# test: Adds missing tests or corrects existing tests.
# chore: Changes to the build process or auxiliary tools and libraries such as documentation generation.
#
# Scope (optional): provides additional contextual information on where the change has taken effect. 
# In eg., a particular component or feature that the change impacts.
#
# Description: summarizes the change to make the commit message stand alone. 
# Imperative form (stating what the commit does rather than what it did)
# 50 characters max
#
